    "https://jobs.lse.ac.uk/V2/UserControls/PrivacyPolicy": {
      "title": "Privacy Policy",
      "description": "Privacy Policy Privacy Policy Register Login We respect your right to privacy. This privacy policy sets out and details the information that we may collect from\nyou and how we may use this information through the engage|ats website (the Service) https://jobs.lse.ac.uk . When you register on the Service, the information you give us will be used: in your application for one or more jobs so we can administer your account, and, if you are an employer, so that jobseekers can contact you for general UK employment trend, vacancy research and analysis purposes. The privacy policy should be read alongside the Employer Terms and Conditions and the Cookie Policy. About us In this privacy policy, the Service is run by Havas People Ltd. through the engage|ats software on behalf of the https://jobs.lse.ac.uk . The https://jobs.lse.ac.uk are the Data Controller of any personal data processed by the Service and described in this privacy policy. Havas People Ltd provide the Service and protect the personal data acting in their role as the Data Processor, alongside Microsoft Azure who also are the data processor (in their role as ISP for the Service). Use of the Service The Service is available to UK jobseekers and employers, 24 hours a day, 7 days a week. Jobseekers can use the Service to apply for jobs and send their CV and other documents to employers who are advertising for jobs. This privacy policy applies only to your use of the Service. You may apply for jobs posted by employers and, if you choose to apply, they may also gather other information about you. If you do apply, you should consult those employer’s privacy policies, as appropriate and applicable. The employer will be the data controller for your personal data, once they receive application data you have sent them, including any additional data they have gathered from you. As part of your Applicant profile you may upload CV’s and other relevant documents to send to employers when applying for jobs through the Service. Each job may have its own document requirements. In your use of the Service, we will, store the results of your jobs searches and job applications within an activity history, so that you can review these at any time. keep a record of when you log into and log out of the Service for dealing with technical queries for example and to provide, maintain, protect and improve the quality of the Service Store the copies of the CV you wish to retain on the service and other so that you can use these to apply for jobs Collection and use of your information When you access the Service via any means we may collect, store and use certain personal information in line with this policy, (specifically the email address of the jobseeker, the application, activity history and the CV data) We may also ask you for additional information when you report a problem with the Service, act in the capacity of an employer or complain about an employer.(e.g. your name or telephone number to ring you) To register or apply for a job on the Service, we will ask for your email address. If you contact us with a query or support request, we may also keep a record of that correspondence. This is so we can link it to any similar correspondence from other users as this will assist us in identifying service improvements. We may also collect data relating to your visits to the Service that cannot identify you but records your use of our Service including, for example, details of how long you have used the Service and the number of jobs that have been applied for and when. We may also collect your computer’s IP address in order to help us improve the delivery of and protect the integrity of the Service. This will not identify you as an individual to us. Storage of information All information is stored on our secure servers, and as part of our data backup process, which store data backups for a maximum of three months. When you register for the Service, we will ask you to choose a password which enables you to access your account. You are responsible for keeping this password confidential. We ask you not to share this password with anyone. You may change this password at anytime. The complexity of the password you choose is determined by https://jobs.lse.ac.uk . In addition, we or our data processors acting on our behalf may also store or process information that we collect about you in countries inside the European Economic Area. The hosting provider for the website and the data associated with the functional delivery of the service is processed within the UK. We have put in place technical and organisational security measures to prevent the loss or unauthorised access of your personal information. However, whilst we have used our best efforts to ensure the security of your data, please be aware that we cannot guarantee the security of information transmitted over the Internet. Legal basis for processing your information Our legal basis for collecting and using the personal information described within this privacy policy is contained within GDPR Article 6(1)(e). Where processing is necessary for the performance of a task carried out in the public interest or in the exercise of official authority vested in the controller https://jobs.lse.ac.uk will collect and use your information. The data processors are not permitted to use the data for any other purpose than enabling Applicants to find work Disclosure of your information We will only disclose your information where we are permitted or required to do so by law, or where necessary to deliver the service. We will not sell or share your data with third parties for marketing purposes. Data retention We retain personal information we collect from you where we have an ongoing legitimate business need to do so (for example, to provide you with the Service you have requested) When we have no ongoing legitimate business need to process your personal information, we will either delete or anonymise it or, if this is not possible (for example, because your personal information has been stored in backup archives), then we will securely store your personal information and isolate it from any further processing until deletion is possible. Please note the maximum database retention period is three months. You may close your Applicant account at any time. Closing your account deletes all the personal information held in your profile, including your CV(s) and other documents you have uploaded onto the Service, with the exception of your account activity history. This process is irreversible so please be aware when deleting your account. Specifically, the account activity history records when you have accessed the service and closed the account. We retain end-user account activity history for months, including on deletion of an account, to protect the interests of individual end-users and the service as a whole, rather than viewing the Applicant data for the purpose of benefit claim administration. - The account activity history records when a jobseeker or employer has accessed the service and undertaken key operations, including login and logout activities, deleting their account, job application actions and uploading or deleting a CV. - We have a legitimate need to retain this data to assist jobseekers who report potential misuse of their account or if we were to suspect systematic abuse of the service as a whole. Your Applicant account and any subsequent applications will be anonymised following  months from the date of first Applicant registration. If any of your applications have not been processed to new application stages in the last months, we will automatically schedule your Applicant account including applications, to be anonymised over the following 24 hours. Using the same email address and Applicant account to register or apply for new job roles will extend your retention period for months. Your Applicant account and any subsequent applications will be anonymised following 18 months  from the date of first Applicant registration. If you have contacted us with a service query, we will delete the records of that contact twelve months after that communication exchange is over. Your rights The right of access and right to rectification: You can see and edit your personal details via your profile page whenever you wish. Right to erasure You can erase your Personal Data at any time. If you receive email alerts, you can delete these within your account or from the link within the emails. If you have an account with a password you can individually delete any CV(s) or other documents you may have uploaded by going to the profile section of your account. You can also delete your entire account from the ‘Manage Account’ section here. The Service may, from time to time, contain links to and from the websites of third parties. If you follow a link to any of these websites, please note that these websites have their own privacy policies. Please check these policies before you submit any personal information to these websites, because your rights may be different. Children We strongly believe in protecting the privacy of children. In line with this belief, we do not knowingly collect or maintain personal information from persons under 13 years of age, and no part of the Service is directed to persons under 13 years of age. If you are under 13 years of age, then please do not use or access the Service at any time or in any manner. Updating this privacy policy We may update or amend this privacy policy from time to time, to comply with law or to meet our changing business requirements. When we update our privacy policy, we will take appropriate measures to inform you, consistent with the significance of the changes we make. Any updates or amendments will be posted on the Service. By continuing to access the Service, accessing and updating your Applicant profile, uploading CVs and applying for jobs, your access and use will be subject to these updates and amendments. The privacy policy terms were last updated on 14th October2022. Contacting https://jobs.lse.ac.uk If you have any questions, comments or complaints about this privacy policy, please contact us here: HR.jobs@lse.ac.uk Login Register Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Password: Sign in Forgot password? Your password has expired, please create a new password below. Your email address has not been verified. Please check your email or click here to resend. Verification email has been resent. Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Reset password Cancel Email Address: New Password: At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm Password: Update Password Your login attempt was not successful. Please try again Please select Baroness Baron Doctor Father Lady Lord Miss Mr Mrs Ms Professor Dame Professor Professor Lord Professor Sir Reverend Sir Other Dame Mx Title * First name * Last name * Email address * Password * At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm password * I have read and understood the terms and conditions I have read and understood the data protection statement Create Account Cancel An email has been sent to your email address. Please confirm that your email address is active by clicking the link in the email. Powered by engage|ats Havas People a Havas Company This site is protected by reCAPTCHA. Contact Us - Application Query Terms and Conditions Privacy Policy Cookies Accessibility FAQs By clicking “Accept All Cookies”, you agree to the storing of cookies on your device to enhance site navigation, analyze site usage, and assist in our marketing efforts. View our privacy policy Cookies Settings Reject All Accept All Cookies Privacy Preference Center When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. This information might be about you, your preferences or your device and is mostly used to make the site work as you expect it to. The information does not usually directly identify you, but it can give you a more personalized web experience. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. Click on the different category headings to find out more and change our default settings. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Allow All Manage Consent Preferences Strictly Necessary Services Always Active These Services are necessary for the website to function and cannot be switched off in our systems. They are usually only set in response to actions made by you which amount to a request for services, such as setting your privacy preferences, logging in or filling in forms. You can set your browser to block or alert you about these cookies, but some parts of the site will not then work. Functional Services Functional Services With these services, the website is able to provide advanced functionality and personalization. They may be set by us or by third parties whose services we use on our sites. If you do not allow these services, this website may not function properly. Back Button Cookie List Search Icon Filter Icon Clear checkbox label label Apply Cancel Consent Leg.Interest checkbox label label checkbox label label checkbox label label Reject All Confirm My Choices 1 Technical Support Today New Messages Technical Support Chatbot (with creds) a few seconds ago Welcome to Technical Support. Please could you let us know whether you're a candidate or a recruiter? Candidate Recruiter ⚡ by Freshworks 1"
    },
    "https://jobs.lse.ac.uk/V2/UserControls/CookieConsent": {
      "title": "CookieConsent",
      "description": "CookieConsent CookieConsent Register Login Cookie Policy for https://jobs.lse.ac.uk/ engage|ats is a software product provided by Havas People . This\nwebsite and the product engage|ats is legally owned by Havas People. When you visit our website https://jobs.lse.ac.uk/ some\ncookies or other tracking technologies may be stored on your device (computer,\ntablet or smartphone). This Cookie Policy contains information on what cookies\nare, the type of cookies used by Havas People on the website https://jobs.lse.ac.uk/ and\nthe purpose of such use, and your choices regarding cookies. This Cookie Policy should be read together with the Privacy policy and Terms and Conditions. Cookie List A cookie is a small piece of data (text file) that a website – when visited by a user – asks your browser to store on your device in order to remember information about you, such as your language preference or login information. Those cookies are set by us and called first-party cookies. We also use third-party cookies – which are cookies from a domain different than the domain of the website you are visiting – for our advertising and marketing efforts. More specifically, we use cookies and other tracking technologies for the following purposes: Strictly Necessary Services These Services are necessary for the website to function and cannot be switched off in our systems. They are usually only set in response to actions made by you which amount to a request for services, such as setting your privacy preferences, logging in or filling in forms. You can set your browser to block or alert you about these cookies, but some parts of the site will not then work. Strictly Necessary Services Cookie Subgroup Cookies Cookies used jobs.lse.ac.uk __RequestVerificationToken , ASP.NET_SessionId , OptanonConsent , OptanonAlertBoxClosed First Party Functional Services With these services, the website is able to provide advanced functionality and personalization. They may be set by us or by third parties whose services we use on our sites. If you do not allow these services, this website may not function properly. Functional Services Cookie Subgroup Cookies Cookies used demosite.engageats.co.uk ApplicationGatewayAffinityCORS Third Party Contact Us If you have any questions regarding this cookie policy please email us at dpo@havaspeople.com. 1.0.0.20 1.0.0.20 Login Register Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Password: Sign in Forgot password? Your password has expired, please create a new password below. Your email address has not been verified. Please check your email or click here to resend. Verification email has been resent. Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Reset password Cancel Email Address: New Password: At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm Password: Update Password Your login attempt was not successful. Please try again Please select Baroness Baron Doctor Father Lady Lord Miss Mr Mrs Ms Professor Dame Professor Professor Lord Professor Sir Reverend Sir Other Dame Mx Title * First name * Last name * Email address * Password * At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm password * I have read and understood the terms and conditions I have read and understood the data protection statement Create Account Cancel An email has been sent to your email address. Please confirm that your email address is active by clicking the link in the email. Powered by engage|ats Havas People a Havas Company This site is protected by reCAPTCHA. Contact Us - Application Query Terms and Conditions Privacy Policy Cookies Accessibility FAQs By clicking “Accept All Cookies”, you agree to the storing of cookies on your device to enhance site navigation, analyze site usage, and assist in our marketing efforts. View our privacy policy Cookies Settings Reject All Accept All Cookies Privacy Preference Center When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. This information might be about you, your preferences or your device and is mostly used to make the site work as you expect it to. The information does not usually directly identify you, but it can give you a more personalized web experience. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. Click on the different category headings to find out more and change our default settings. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Allow All Manage Consent Preferences Strictly Necessary Services Always Active These Services are necessary for the website to function and cannot be switched off in our systems. They are usually only set in response to actions made by you which amount to a request for services, such as setting your privacy preferences, logging in or filling in forms. You can set your browser to block or alert you about these cookies, but some parts of the site will not then work. Functional Services Functional Services With these services, the website is able to provide advanced functionality and personalization. They may be set by us or by third parties whose services we use on our sites. If you do not allow these services, this website may not function properly. Back Button Cookie List Search Icon Filter Icon Clear checkbox label label Apply Cancel Consent Leg.Interest checkbox label label checkbox label label checkbox label label Reject All Confirm My Choices 1 Technical Support Today New Messages Technical Support Chatbot (with creds) a few seconds ago Welcome to Technical Support. Please could you let us know whether you're a candidate or a recruiter? Candidate Recruiter ⚡ by Freshworks 1"
